# Astro Linux — source-build overrides for binary packages-mode
#
# In binary packages-mode (docs/03 §1 "Binary consumption for dev builds"),
# the packages stage builds from source ONLY:
#   1. templates present in astro-cports/ (Astro's own collection),
#   2. cports templates shadowed/patched via build/patches/cports/*.patch
#      (detected automatically from the patch file paths),
#   3. anything listed here.
# Everything else is installed at rootfs time from Chimera's signed binary
# repository. Source packages-mode (release/nightly) ignores this file and
# builds the full manifest from source.
#
# One package name per line (bare template name, e.g. "musl" — the
# main/ vs user/ collection is resolved automatically). '#' comments.
